This extension adds System Shock 2 (Classic AND 25th Anniversary Remaster) modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Converts legacy SS2 mods for Remaster.[/summary]

Converts legacy SS2 mods for the Remaster.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Mods with a ".kpf" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Converted Legacy mods with an "obj", "mesh", "bitmap", "motions", "sq_scripts", "sdn2" or one of 5 other named folders and a ".dml", ".gam" or ".mis" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "mods" or "cutscenes" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries / Root Folder mods with a "mods" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Classic mods are supported.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[/list]

Remaster:
[list]
[*]Legacy SS2 mods with recognizable folders and file extensions will be converted to .kpf format automatically. System Shock 2 is listed as a compatible download domain.[/*]
[/list]
[size=3]Classic:[/size]
[list]
[*]Prompts the user to download and run the SS2Tool installer on first startup (enables modding and installs Blue Mod Manager).[/*]
[*]Installs mods with recognizable folders and file extensions to a 'DMM' folder. Blue Mod Manager is then used to complete the installation of mods and launch the game.[/*]
[*]Launches the game via Blue Mod Manager (installed by SS2Tool).[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for System Shock 2 (Classic AND 25th Anniversary Remaster) mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mod .kpf:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".kpf" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Converted Legacy Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "obj", "mesh", "bitmap", "motions", "sq_scripts", "sdn2", "strings", "iface", "intrface", "misdml" or "snd" folder and a ".dml", ".gam" or ".mis" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Root Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "mods" or "cutscenes" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── mods\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "mods" or "cutscenes" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Classic Mod:

Handled by the "testClassic" installer. Inspect the extension source for the exact archive layout it expects.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
